    z10_qwen_two_pools_r2    1 passed   437.29 s
    z11_qwen_two_pools_r3    1 passed   272.24 s

D-C14 (the hang the paragraph below names) was fixed at faec6e59938 and is qualified; behind
it was D-C15, a DRAM retention defect with nothing to do with the clash - close() never
released the layer weights, 398 617 984 B per bank at 80 layers - fixed at 299440bb276. See
D-C14.status and D-C15.status.

So all three claims the Llama L1 address clash blocked are measured:
    area 1, block-level cross-slot isolation   i1b/i2b/i3b   3/3
    area 3, chunked prefill                    k1b/k2b/k3b   3/3
    two models in one process                  z6/z8/z9      3/3   (this attempt)

ALSO NOTE, for anyone reading `c-exec-llama`'s account of this defect: that job ran at
commit 2b463f17fcd and EXITED at 2026-08-30T00:02Z, while the clash fix landed at
32e552bb0b2 on 2026-08-31 11:32. Its "prefill after a decode" reproduction, its three
addresses (543488, 542016, 544832) and its conclusion that the clash blocks serving are all
PRE-FIX measurements. Attempt 6 re-asks them at HEAD (queue q12).

--- superseded paragraph, kept for the record ---
THE THIRD BLOCKED CLAIM IS NOT MEASURED. `test_qwen_two_paged_pools_agree_and_a_contiguous
_cache_is_unreachable` (two models in one process) no longer hits the clash and no longer
hits D-C13's OOM - it now HANGS, at the second model's first decode, on a distinct defect
(D-C14: the ttnn program cache is per mesh device and outlives a model, so two identical
models share compiled decode programs and therefore the first model's global-CB addresses).
D-C14's fix is implemented and host-qualified; it is NOT on silicon, because the mesh lost
board 23 to POST_RESET at 11:10Z and ten reset attempts across four mechanisms did not
recover it.

Fix: commit 32e552bb0b2. `release_global_cb_on_prefill` is now the default for both Galaxy
models (forced by arithmetic: 869 056 B of L1 above the prefill CB region end against
127 776 + 792 256 = 920 032 B needed, so the buffer and a prefill program of this shape
cannot coexist on any allocation order), plus `global_cb_headroom` and
`Prefetcher2D._allocate_global_cb`, which holds every free L1 gap above the low region,
reproduces the free-region top the first creation saw, and raises if the creation's blocks
move. Tests: test_prefetcher_2d.py 33 passed, 22 before; removing only the gap-filling pass
fails exactly the two gap cases.
